# Expo / EAS build artifacts and native projects (regenerated by prebuild/build)
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
# 🔴 ANCHORED, deliberately. These two were bare `ios/` and `android/`, which
# match a directory of that name at ANY depth - including
# `modules/*/ios/`, where a local Expo module's Swift source lives. That is not
# a build artifact, it is source, and the bare pattern silently excluded it:
# the file existed on disk, `git add -A` skipped it, and an EAS build (which
# archives from git) would have shipped a binary with the native module
# missing while every local check stayed green.
/ios/
/android/
expo-env.d.ts
*.orig.*
